1
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,070
The power of one person
does not amount to much.

2
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:26,960
As such, I will do all I can,

3
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,210
however little that may be,

4
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:31,550
to protect those who are dear to me.

5
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:38,010
Those below me will protect those below them.

6
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:41,430
We tiny humans should be
able to do that much, at least.

7
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:44,440
Geometric progression, huh?

8
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:46,400
Which means...

9
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,980
in order for you to protect the whole country,

10
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:52,400
you'll have to be standing
at the top of the pyramid.

11
00:00:54,030 --> 00:00:58,530
I'll bet it feels awfully
good to be there, Hughes.

12
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:03,580
But I won't be able to
climb that high all by myself.

13
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:05,460
I'm sure of that much.

14
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:09,540
What are you swaggering on about?

15
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:13,300
This could be interesting.
I'll take a piece of that action.

16
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:18,300
I want to see how your naïve
idealism changes this country.

17
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:25,600
Colonel...

18
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,060
Colonel!

19
00:01:29,270 --> 00:01:33,280
If you're tired, why don't
you go to the nap room?

20
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:37,070
Sorry. I want to gather up
all the unfinished paperwork

21
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:40,330
before we transfer to Central.

22
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:42,450
I haven't slept much lately.

23
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:45,830
You seemed to be having a dream.

24
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:49,380
Oh, it was just an insignificant old memory.

25
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:55,800
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

26
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,180
mada jinsei nagai desho?

27
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:00,850
Yarinokoshite'ru koto

28
00:02:00,850 --> 00:02:04,680
yarinaoshite mitai kara

29
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:21,030
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

30
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:27,080
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

31
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:30,250
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai no

32
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:33,880
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

33
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,420
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

34
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:40,680
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

35
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,350
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo

36
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:44,140
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

37
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:45,770
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni

38
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:47,560
dare wo matte'ru no?

39
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,190
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni

40
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:51,020
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

41
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,560
Nani kara nogaretai n da

42
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:54,070
...genjitsu tte yatsu?

43
00:02:54,070 --> 00:02:57,360
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte

44
00:02:57,360 --> 00:03:00,950
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

45
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:06,080
Bunan ni nante yatte'rarenai kara

46
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,870
...kaeru basho mo nai no

47
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:11,080
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

48
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:14,630
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

49
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:16,500
Natsukashiku naru

50
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,720
konna itami mo kangei jan

51
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:26,560
So, I don't remember
anything after this one kicked me.

52
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:30,310
Guardians who were only
souls, a precious sacrifice,

53
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:32,270
and him letting you live...

54
00:03:32,270 --> 00:03:36,230
Uroboros tattoos, a
Philosopher's Stone transmutation circle,

55
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:40,820
and Mr. Marcoh saying
they used Stones in Ishval...

56
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:44,490
There are too many mysteries
here for just a simple experiment.

57
00:03:44,490 --> 00:03:49,830
And there's no way to investigate any further,
what with the lab being a pile of rubble.

58
00:03:49,370 --> 00:03:51,330
"Hmm..."

59
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:56,290
It sounds like they're talking
about something pretty thorny.

60
00:03:56,290 --> 00:03:59,510
I don't want to stick my nose
into anything any more dangerous,

61
00:03:59,510 --> 00:04:00,880
so I'm not listening!

62
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:03,260
Ah, you there,

63
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:07,310
is this where the Fullmetal Alchemist's room is?

64
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:09,220
Yes, this is--

65
00:04:10,270 --> 00:04:13,060
If I root around in the criminal
lists at the court-martial office,

66
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:15,730
something might turn up.

67
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:19,650
I shall look into those who
were working under Dr. Marcoh

68
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:23,030
in researching the Stone.

69
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:28,240
Excuse me.

70
00:04:30,410 --> 00:04:34,370
F-Fuhrer King Bradley!

71
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:37,880
Ah, keep your voice down. As you were.

72
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,840
Your Excellency, what are you doing here?

73
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:45,430
What, you ask?
Visiting a sick friend. Do you like melons?

74
00:04:45,430 --> 00:04:47,850
Yeah, thanks.

75
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:49,810
I mean...!

76
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:53,060
I understand you've been
checking up on the senior staff members,

77
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,440
Major Armstrong.

78
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:59,070
Sir? Um, er, sir, how did you...

79
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:02,490
Don't underestimate my information network.

80
00:05:02,490 --> 00:05:06,610
And Edward Elric...

81
00:05:06,610 --> 00:05:09,080
the Philosopher's Stone?

82
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:14,870
What have you found out?
Depending on how much you've learned...

83
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:26,180
Just kidding!

84
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:28,180
You needn't be so defensive!

85
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:30,100
Huh?

86
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:34,390
I know that there is some
unrest among the ranks.

87
00:05:34,390 --> 00:05:37,400
I think that something must be done about it.

88
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,360
Ah, that's just...

89
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:43,440
A list of those who were
researching the Philosopher's Stone.

90
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:46,860
All of these men have gone missing.

91
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:48,110
Sir?

92
00:05:48,110 --> 00:05:51,990
They disappeared several days
before the 5th Laboratory collapsed.

93
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:54,910
The enemy is always a step ahead of us.

94
00:05:54,910 --> 00:05:57,500
And even with my information network,

95
00:05:57,500 --> 00:06:01,090
as it currently stands,
I have no handle on the enemy's size,

96
00:06:01,090 --> 00:06:05,220
their objectives, or how
far they've penetrated us.

97
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:09,140
In other words, it's quite
dangerous to be poking around.

98
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:10,640
Mm-hmm.

99
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:15,810
Lt. Colonel Hughes,
Major Armstrong, Elric brothers,

100
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:19,980
I've determined you to be men that I can trust.

101
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:22,520
I will not permit you to stick your noses

102
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:25,740
any further into this matter,
nor speak of it to anyone!

103
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:29,070
Under the present circumstances,
when we can't tell friend from foe,

104
00:06:29,070 --> 00:06:32,120
you cannot trust anyone!

105
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:36,250
Consider everyone in the military
to be the enemy, and act discreetly!

106
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:38,750
However...

107
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:42,340
when the time comes,
I will have much work for you to do,

108
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:43,840
so see that you are ready.

109
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,050
Yes, sir!

110
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:48,510
Excellency!
Where is His Excellency, the Fuhrer?!

111
00:06:48,510 --> 00:06:52,510
Uh-oh, my pesky
subordinates have come after me.

112
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,730
I secretly slipped out of work, you see.

113
00:06:57,730 --> 00:06:59,850
Well, farewell!

114
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:07,780
Ed! Huh...?

115
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:10,070
What's wrong, everyone?

116
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:13,780
Nothing, a storm just passed through.

117
00:07:15,990 --> 00:07:18,750
I bought the tickets you asked me to.

118
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:21,080
The train tomorrow at noon is okay, right?

119
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:23,130
Yeah. Thank you.

120
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:27,420
My, you sure are on the go.
You haven't even completely healed.

121
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:31,800
You expect me to stay in this
disinfectant-reeking place forever?

122
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,430
Where are you going now? Dublith?

123
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:38,600
Yeah. I talked it over with Al,

124
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:42,560
and we're going to go see our teacher.

125
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:45,360
I sure am scared, Brother!

126
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:47,860
I'm sure she's gonna kill us!

127
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:51,990
D-Don't wimp out,
little brother! I'm scared, too!

128
00:07:51,990 --> 00:07:54,740
Who is this teacher of yours?

129
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:58,290
Still quite a distance beyond Dublith.

130
00:07:58,290 --> 00:07:59,830
Whereabouts?

131
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:04,710
Let's see... here.
Right in the middle of the southern area.

132
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:10,340
W-What?!

133
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:13,680
Here! Here! Just before Dublith!

134
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:17,100
The holy land of automail, Rush Valley!

135
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:19,180
I've always wanted to go there!

136
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:22,140
Take me! Take me! Take me! Take me!

137
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:24,350
Go there on your own.

138
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:26,520
But who will pay my traveling expenses?

139
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:27,980
Are you trying to mooch off of me?

140
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:31,190
Now, now, where's the harm?
It's on our way, and all.

141
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:32,570
If you insist.

142
00:08:32,570 --> 00:08:34,610
Hooray!

143
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:38,870
I'll go call Grandma!

144
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:43,460
She'd make a fine wife.

145
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:44,670
Don't tell me!

146
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:48,630
Though, not as fine as my own wife!

147
00:08:49,590 --> 00:08:52,300
Okay, Papa's heading out now!

148
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:55,510
Papa, are you coming home early today?

149
00:08:55,510 --> 00:09:00,220
Hmm, I'm not sure. Papa has a lot of work to do.

150
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:03,480
But I'll come home as soon as I can.

151
00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:08,150
--That tickles!
--You're going to be late.

152
00:09:08,150 --> 00:09:11,030
Winry, you're leaving today, right?

153
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:15,660
I won't be able to come
see you off, so take care.

154
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:19,620
Mr. Hughes, thanks so much for everything.

155
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:23,710
Whenever you're in Central,
be sure to come visit us.

156
00:09:23,710 --> 00:09:25,710
Consider our home as your home.

157
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:28,460
Also, give my regards to the guys, okay?

158
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:29,340
Right.

159
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:31,550
Papa, work hard!

160
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:33,380
Come home safe!

161
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:46,560
What made you suddenly
decide to go see your teacher?

162
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:48,860
There are two reasons.

163
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:51,690
Lately, we've been on a real losing streak.

164
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:54,820
Huh? You're going there because
you want to improve your fighting?

165
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,650
What are you, fighting fools?

166
00:09:56,650 --> 00:10:00,120
No, dumbass, it's not as simple as that!

167
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:03,870
It's not just the fighting,
it's what's inside us, you might say.

168
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:04,660
Right?

169
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:08,250
Yeah. Anyhow, we feel like
if we go see our teacher,

170
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:10,630
it will help to strengthen us somehow.

171
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:13,800
I want to get even stronger.

172
00:10:16,930 --> 00:10:19,010
What's the second reason?

173
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:22,140
To ask our teacher about
the Philosopher's Stone.

174
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:25,350
The truth within the truth.

175
00:10:25,350 --> 00:10:28,060
We never did end up figuring out what it was.

176
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:31,190
Our teacher might know something about it.

177
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:34,480
We can't afford to be
concerned about appearances.

178
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:38,700
We have to be ready for
Teacher to kill us, and ask her...

179
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:42,160
ask her... ask her...

180
00:10:42,990 --> 00:10:45,160
Our lives sure have been short, huh?

181
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:48,580
I wish I could have at least found a girlfriend.

182
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:51,130
What kind of teacher do you have...?

183
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:54,170
The Liore insurgency?

184
00:10:54,170 --> 00:10:57,420
Yes, where that new
religion "Letoism" or whatever

185
00:10:57,420 --> 00:11:02,930
was suckering the people.
Sounds like it's finally under control.

186
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:05,520
Between Ishval and these insurgencies,

187
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:07,770
the eastern area is
having a rough time of it, huh?

188
00:11:07,770 --> 00:11:09,350
It's not just the eastern area.

189
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:13,190
There are uprisings and border
skirmishes in the north and west, too.

190
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:16,070
The bodies are piling up all over, are they?

191
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:18,900
The government might just
be overthrown before too long.

192
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,120
Colonel, where are you going?

193
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:29,410
I'm running over to the archive room.

194
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:35,170
Liore...

195
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:38,760
uprisings all over... The Philosopher's Stone...

196
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:41,050
ingredients are humans...

197
00:11:41,050 --> 00:11:45,010
what we did in Ishval...

198
00:11:45,010 --> 00:11:51,020
Hey, now, who was it that came up with this?

199
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,310
I have to tell the Fuhrer, quickly...

200
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:58,610
It's a pleasure to meet you, Lt. Colonel Hughes.

201
00:11:58,610 --> 00:12:03,950
Or perhaps I should say, "farewell."

202
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:19,130
Cool tattoo you've got there.

203
00:12:19,130 --> 00:12:22,510
You've learned too much, Lt. Colonel Hughes.

204
00:12:38,610 --> 00:12:40,940
Damn!

205
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:50,120
"Damn"? That's what I was going to say.

206
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,870
Oh my, Lt. Colonel Hughes.

207
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:57,420
Here to call and brag
about your family some more--

208
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:58,960
Colonel, you're bleeding!

209
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:02,380
It's nothing! I need the phone!

210
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,840
The prefectural office...

211
00:13:12,890 --> 00:13:15,060
Sorry to have bothered you.

212
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:16,940
Eh? Colonel!

213
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:19,270
Yes, Eastern Command Center.

214
00:13:19,270 --> 00:13:22,690
Put me through to Colonel Roy... Mustang.

215
00:13:22,690 --> 00:13:25,240
We have a rule against
connecting anyone from an outside line.

216
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:27,570
This is Lt. Colonel Hughes, in Central!

217
00:13:27,570 --> 00:13:29,450
I'm calling from outside
because it's an emergency!

218
00:13:29,450 --> 00:13:30,870
Your code, please.

219
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:33,370
Ah, geez, what a pain!

220
00:13:33,790 --> 00:13:39,880
Uncle, Sugar, Oliver, Eight, Zero, Zero!

221
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:42,760
Code verified. Just a moment, please.

222
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:46,180
Hurry it up! The military is in trouble!

223
00:13:50,810 --> 00:13:54,310
Would you mind putting
the receiver down, Lt. Colonel?

224
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:58,650
Come on, put it down.

225
00:13:58,650 --> 00:14:00,570
Lieutenant Ross?

226
00:14:00,570 --> 00:14:03,780
No, it isn't. Who are you?

227
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:06,610
I'm 2nd Lieutenant Maria Ross.
Have you forgotten?

228
00:14:06,610 --> 00:14:08,990
No you're not.

229
00:14:08,990 --> 00:14:14,080
Lieutenant Ross has a mole under her left eye!

230
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:19,080
Oh, is that right? How careless of me.

231
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:23,710
Is this better?

232
00:14:23,710 --> 00:14:27,760
What is this?
It's like I'm dreaming or something.

233
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:31,510
It's awfully unfortunate for
you that your mind works so fast,

234
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:32,970
Lt. Colonel Hughes.

235
00:14:32,970 --> 00:14:35,480
Hey, now, have a heart.

236
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:40,190
I have a wife and daughter
waiting for me at home. I can't go

237
00:14:40,190 --> 00:14:42,110
dying here!

238
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:48,360
Nice rendering, huh?

239
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:50,160
You son of a bitch!

240
00:14:57,660 --> 00:15:01,130
Call from Lt. Colonel Hughes,
in Central, on a public line.

241
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:03,800
Again? Put him through.

242
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:07,880
I'm here. If you're bragging about
your daughter, I'm not listening.

243
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:11,970
Hughes...?

244
00:15:11,970 --> 00:15:15,720
Hughes... Hey, Hughes!

245
00:15:22,110 --> 00:15:24,940
You humans really are such fools.

246
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:28,190
You risk your lives over
the most pointless things.

247
00:15:35,030 --> 00:15:41,290
Elicia... Gracia... I'm sorry...

248
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:46,840
I promised... I'd be home... early...

249
00:15:52,970 --> 00:15:55,260
Oh, this is good!

250
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:57,720
This apple pie is the best!

251
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,810
Mrs. Gracia is a very good cook.

252
00:16:00,810 --> 00:16:02,310
I know.

253
00:16:02,310 --> 00:16:06,730
The quiche she made for us
before was also awfully delicious.

254
00:16:06,730 --> 00:16:10,900
I put it on the list of things
I want to eat when I get my body back.

255
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:14,160
She taught me how to make it,
so once you get your body back, Al,

256
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,280
I'll make it for you.

257
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:17,450
All right!

258
00:16:18,330 --> 00:16:21,960
Mr. Hughes and Mrs. Gracia
were both really great people.

259
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:25,540
Colonel Hughes is a doting father, a busybody,

260
00:16:25,540 --> 00:16:27,960
and annoying to be around.

261
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:31,550
He did always come by your hospital room
to give you a hard time, huh, Brother?

262
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:33,340
Seriously.

263
00:16:35,510 --> 00:16:37,890
He said he was busy with work,

264
00:16:37,890 --> 00:16:40,350
but he would always come to visit me.

265
00:16:40,350 --> 00:16:42,980
Next time we're there,
we ought to thank him somehow.

266
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:44,230
Yeah.

267
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,140
Mama,

268
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:21,270
why are they burying Papa?

269
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:22,890
Elicia...

270
00:17:22,890 --> 00:17:27,560
If they do that, Papa
won't be able to do his work.

271
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:28,940
Elici--

272
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:34,570
Papa said he had a lot of work to do.

273
00:17:34,570 --> 00:17:36,360
No!

274
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,780
Don't bury him!

275
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:40,740
Papa!

276
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:46,290
Promoted two grades
for dying in the line of duty...

277
00:17:46,290 --> 00:17:49,750
Brigadier General Hughes, huh?

278
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:53,130
What good does it do to have someone
who said they'd support me from below

279
00:17:53,130 --> 00:17:58,140
get above me, you idiot?

280
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:00,010
Colonel...

281
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:08,400
Alchemists are nasty creatures,
aren't they, Lieutenant?

282
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:11,770
There's a part of me that
was just frantically piecing together

283
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:15,740
the theories of human transmutation in my head.

284
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:19,490
I think I can now
understand what those boys felt

285
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:21,660
when they tried to transmute their mother.

286
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:27,420
Are you all right?

287
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:29,920
Yes, I'm all right.

288
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:33,840
Oh no, it's started to rain.

289
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,970
No, there's no rain--

290
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:42,470
Yes, it's raining.

291
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:50,520
Y-Yes, you're right.
Let's go back. It's chilly out here.

292
00:18:52,150 --> 00:18:55,320
He left, saying he was
going to the archive room.

293
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:58,450
That was the last time I saw the colonel.

294
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:02,410
Did he get into a fight with someone?

295
00:19:02,410 --> 00:19:04,160
Probably.

296
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,950
There were traces of blood

297
00:19:05,950 --> 00:19:08,670
leading from inside the
room out into the hallway.

298
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:11,960
And the next place he went was...

299
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:16,010
The colonel was hurt,
and was about to place a call,

300
00:19:16,010 --> 00:19:21,050
but then he didn't call anyone, and just left.

301
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:25,930
He picked up on something
in the court-martial office,

302
00:19:25,930 --> 00:19:28,140
and even though he
could have called from inside,

303
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:32,650
he deliberately went
outside to try to contact me.

304
00:19:32,650 --> 00:19:35,020
The Eastern Command Center
switchboard operator

305
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:38,780
heard Hughes say "The military is in trouble!"

306
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:43,620
What was it? What was he trying to tell me?

307
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:46,910
Colonel...

308
00:19:46,910 --> 00:19:50,080
I've brought Major Armstrong.

309
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:57,260
We have some suspects as to those
who murdered Lt. Colonel Hughes.

310
00:19:57,260 --> 00:19:59,590
Then why aren't you out
there catching them, right now?!

311
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:05,390
We have some suspects,
but we don't know who they are.

312
00:20:05,390 --> 00:20:08,810
What do you mean? Explain yourself.

313
00:20:08,810 --> 00:20:10,100
I cannot.

314
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:13,100
I am a colonel, and
I'm telling you to explain it!

315
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,610
Are you going to disobey a superior officer?!

316
00:20:15,610 --> 00:20:17,440
I cannot tell you.

317
00:20:21,950 --> 00:20:25,030
All right. I'm sorry to have called you out.

318
00:20:25,030 --> 00:20:26,240
You're free to go.

319
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:27,830
Yes, sir.

320
00:20:31,370 --> 00:20:34,830
Come to think of it,
I forgot to mention something.

321
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:39,590
The Elric brothers were here
up until just a few days ago.

322
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:41,130
The Elric brothers?

323
00:20:41,130 --> 00:20:45,470
Yes, the Elric brothers.

324
00:20:45,470 --> 00:20:47,930
Did they find what they were looking for?

325
00:20:47,930 --> 00:20:52,940
No. After all, it is an
item of legendary proportions.

326
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:56,400
I see. Thanks.

327
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:00,860
Not much information
to be gathered from that, is there?

328
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:05,240
Man, I tell you,
the major is far too unsuspecting.

329
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:08,200
He said "those who killed Hughes,"

330
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,120
which would mean there is
more than one person involved.

331
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:15,380
It could be that there are
people working as a group.

332
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:17,210
The fact that he wouldn't tell me anything,

333
00:21:17,210 --> 00:21:20,760
even though as a colonel I ordered him to,

334
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:25,010
means that there is someone
above me who has forbidden him to talk.

335
00:21:25,010 --> 00:21:28,430
Someone to do with the senior staff, I'll bet.

336
00:21:28,430 --> 00:21:32,270
And what the Elric brothers are looking for--

337
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:36,020
which is to say, the Philosopher's Stone.

338
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:39,820
So how is an organization having
to do with the senior military staff,

339
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:43,490
connected to the
Philosopher's Stone and Lt. Colonel Hughes?

340
00:21:43,490 --> 00:21:45,780
I don't know yet.

341
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:48,700
But once I transfer to Central,

342
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:51,330
I'm going to make sure
to investigate the senior staff,

343
00:21:51,330 --> 00:21:53,620
and smoke out whoever killed Hughes.

344
00:21:53,620 --> 00:21:56,580
It's not like you to mix
public and private affairs.

345
00:21:56,580 --> 00:21:58,840
There's nothing "public" or "private" about it.

346
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:01,300
All of this, whether
taking the position of Fuhrer

347
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:06,510
or avenging Hughes,
I do of my own personal volition!

348
00:22:06,510 --> 00:22:09,930
I'm going to stick it to the
senior staff. Are you coming?

349
00:22:09,930 --> 00:22:12,060
After all this time, you have to ask?

350
00:22:27,450 --> 00:22:33,290
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

351
00:22:33,290 --> 00:22:38,580
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

352
00:22:38,580 --> 00:22:44,460
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

353
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:49,220
futari yorisotta

354
00:22:52,510 --> 00:22:57,850
Muri na egao no ura

355
00:22:57,850 --> 00:23:03,190
nobita kage o kakumau

356
00:23:03,190 --> 00:23:12,910
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

357
00:23:14,580 --> 00:23:22,210
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

358
00:23:25,210 --> 00:23:30,550
kuuhaku no yoru mo kuru hazu no nai asa mo

359
00:23:30,550 --> 00:23:34,890
zenbu wakatte'tan da

360
00:23:34,890 --> 00:23:40,600
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

361
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:45,570
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

362
00:23:45,570 --> 00:23:51,280
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

363
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:56,120
futari arukidasu

364
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:03,540
Chasing the young girl Paninya,
who stole his silver watch,

365
00:24:03,540 --> 00:24:06,840
Ed and the others dash through Rush Valley,

366
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:12,180
not knowing what lay in store for them.

367
00:24:12,180 --> 00:24:16,850
Next time on Hagane no Renkinjutsushi:
Fullmetal Alchemist,

368
00:24:16,850 --> 00:24:20,560
Episode 11: "Miracle at Rush Valley."

369
00:24:21,980 --> 00:24:26,440
Were the words the boy engraved
his resolve, or something else?
